4. Repair-catalogue ideas — Command Code
----------------------------------------

What is borrowed: the harness-engineering ideas documented in Command Code's
public docs and reimplemented in internal/tools/repair.go — validate-then-
repair on every tool call, a small catalogue of the failure classes that
actually dominate open-weight models (`null-for-optional`, stringified numbers,
missing required keys, unescaped JSON in arguments, fence-wrapped calls),
per-(model, tool, class) repair telemetry, duplicate-failure loop breaking, and
the cache-stability rule for the compiled prompt prefix (byte-identical above
the task layer, no timestamps in system prompts).

Why attribution only: these are documented behaviours, reimplemented
independently. Command Code's repository license was recorded as *unverified* in
ROADMAP.md, which is exactly why the borrow map restricts this project to
ideas-from-docs: no code was read into this tree, and the ideas themselves are
not copyrightable expression.


5. Memory and skills layout ideas — oh-my-pi (MIT)
--------------------------------------------------

What is borrowed: layout and workflow ideas from oh-my-pi — a local markdown
memory store with dated, append-only lessons; skills as markdown files with a
name/description front matter that are listed and injected on demand; memory
verbs over that store; an agent hub for background worker runs; and
operator-authored stream rules. Reflected in internal/memory/, internal/skills/
and internal/subagent/.

Why attribution only: oh-my-pi is MIT-licensed, and MIT's condition attaches to
copies of the software. AgentForge contains no oh-my-pi code — the file
layouts and verb names are conventions, reimplemented here. The credit is
recorded anyway, so the lineage of the design is not misread as invention.


6. Repository map idea — aider (Apache-2.0)
-------------------------------------------

What is borrowed: the *idea* of a token-budgeted repository map — rank the
repo's symbols, emit the highest-value ones as a compact tree/outline into the
prompt, and stay inside a token budget — implemented in internal/tools/
repomap.go, and the related plan-then-edit split (read-only architect phase,
then an edit phase with the plan injected) in internal/forge/architect.go.

Why attribution only: aider is Apache-2.0. AgentForge's implementation is its
own and shares no code with aider, so no Apache-2.0 §4 notice obligation
attaches; the attribution is for the concept.


